# NOTICE — attribution, data terms, and third-party licences

`job-hunt-kit` is MIT-licensed; see `LICENSE`. This file records the obligations that come with the
*data* it fetches and the *code* it depends on, because neither is covered by that licence.

## Data sources that require attribution

Five of the sources in `research/sources/` publish terms that require naming them wherever their data
appears. **The obligation is enforced in code rather than documented here and hoped for**: each
source stamps its attribution line onto every record it emits, `research/sources/__init__.py` drops
any record that arrives without one, and `attribution_lines()` is what the market report prints. A
report therefore cannot omit an attribution by forgetting to — it would have to strip the line first.

| source | line it stamps |
|---|---|
| Adzuna | `Job data from Adzuna (https://www.adzuna.com)` |
| Himalayas | `Job data from Himalayas (https://himalayas.app)` |
| Remotive | `Job data from Remotive (https://remotive.com), linked back to its Remotive listing` |
| GSA CALC+ | `Source: GSA CALC+ / Contract-Awarded Labor Category (buy.gsa.gov/pricing), US Government public-domain data.` |
| US BLS OEWS | `Source: US Bureau of Labor Statistics, Occupational Employment and Wage Statistics (OEWS), api.bls.gov — US Government public-domain data.` |

The two government sources are public-domain data and the attribution is a courtesy plus a
provenance record; the three job boards require it. The six staffing-agency scrapers in
`core/scrapers/` carry no published attribution requirement and are deliberately absent from that
list.

Remotive's API terms forbid republishing its rows as listings, so it is registered as **market
supply only** — it feeds the aggregate report and is never a job channel. Adzuna's salary figures are
model *predictions* rather than posted pay, and are labelled as such wherever they surface.

## Per-user API keys only

**Every key this tool uses is yours, obtained under your own account and subject to that provider's
terms.** Nothing here ships a key, proxies a key, or shares one between users; there is no hosted
service and no second account. `.env.example` lists the variable names and nothing else, and `.env`
is gitignored. If a source's terms don't permit your use of it, don't set its key — every keyed
source logs one line and returns nothing when its key is unset, and the keyless path is the default.

## No cached source data is committed

Fetched postings, scored judgments and the retrieval index live under `data/`, which is gitignored
and is excluded from publication by name. What a clone gets is the code and the fictional-seeker
example — never a cache of anyone else's listings.

